            <encodings>
              <lod column='[federated.1jbdp9i0boo3cg12fgxcb0trnkks].[sum:orders_all:qk]' />
            </encodings>
            <customized-tooltip>
              <formatted-text>
                <run>If &apos;</run>
                <run bold='true'>All Orders</run>
                <run>&apos; is selected the Rate is calculated as follows:
	*Numerator:  the # of orders within the condition. If the order falls in more than one of the non-seamless order conditions, we assign it to only one following the next priority: Cancelled &gt; Not on time &gt; Service ABC. For example, if an order was canceled and On-Time, the order counts toward the % Failed Rate and not for % Order On Time.
	* Denominator: all the Own Delivery orders within the selected filters. 

If &apos;</run>
                <run bold='true'>Related Orders</run>
                <run>&apos; is selected, the rate is calculated as follows:
	* Numerator: the # of orders within the non-seamless metrics. 
	* Denominator: the Own Delivery orders existing in the Service from which the metric is taken (Cancelled - Vendor, Contacts - Service,...).</run>
              </formatted-text>
            </customized-tooltip>
            <style>
              <style-rule element='mark'>
                <format attr='shape' value='Bug Tracking/light.png' />
                <format attr='size' value='1.6591712236404419' />
              </style-rule>
